=== SURVEY (web source of truth, parity manifest, locked catalog, existing native code) ===
WEB_SOURCE web/src/features/watch/pages/WatchFacePage.tsx:
    A chrome-less PWA route '/watch' tuned for 40-45mm displays (battery ring, range, state badge,
    charging ETA, lock/climate/sentry tap actions, last-updated). It is a RESPONSIVE WEB ROUTE rendered
    in a browser/PWA — NOT a native wearable application.
PARITY_MANIFEST apps/parity/parity-manifest.json — every watch unit is a PHONE surface:
    - route:/watch                              (requiredCount 1)
    - page:watch/WatchFace                      (states: loading, success ; requiredCount 2)
    - api:watch/WatchFace#useWatchSummary       (requiredCount 1)
    - api:watch/WatchFace#useWatchCommand       (requiredCount 1)
    There is NO 'wear' / 'wearable' parity unit. The manifest is generated by P1/S0 from a web/src scan;
    web/src contains no wearable target, so none was emitted. The Android parity owner of the watch
    FEATURE is the A7 phone page (page:watch/WatchFace), not a separate wearable app.
SHARED_CORE (KMP, P1/S8-0059): apps/shared/core/.../presentation/watch/WatchStore.kt + WatchModels.kt and
    data/repo/WatchRepository.kt + HttpWatchRepository.kt exist — watch-summary state/repo is available
    cross-platform via the shared core (would back the A7 phone page when it is built).
ANDROID_APP (namespace io.teslasync.android): modules present = auth, components, data, messaging,
    navigation, notifications, push, settings, shortcuts, ui, widgets.
    - settings.gradle.kts includes ONLY :android (+ composite-build :shared). No :wear module/source set.
    - apps/android/gradle/libs.versions.toml has NO Wear deps: no androidx.wear.compose, no
      com.google.android.horologist, no play-services-wearable (Wear Data Layer).
    - AndroidManifest.xml declares NO <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.type.watch"> and no
      wearable components/services.
    - grep over apps/ for horologist|androidx.wear|play-services-wearable|WearApp|MessageClient|DataClient|
      CapabilityClient => 0 matches.
    - A7 phone WatchFacePage (com/teslasync/watch/WatchFacePage.kt) NOT implemented; no WatchSummary widget.
ADR-002 (native-per-platform, Accepted) platform matrix:
    Windows=WinUI3 ; Android=Jetpack Compose / Material 3 ; macOS+iOS+iPadOS=SwiftUI.
    Wear OS is NOT an accepted platform target.
ADR-012 (version lock, Accepted) + apps/versions.lock.md: the locked Android stack is Compose+M3, AGP,
    Navigation, Maps Compose, Vico. No Wear Compose / Horologist / Data Layer. "Floating 'latest' with no
    pin" is a rejected alternative; "major bumps get a superseding ADR."
README p3-android: A6 is "(reserved) widgets/wear"; only the activated half — Glance home-screen widgets —
    shipped (A8-0001 DONE). The Wear half was never scoped into the manifest, the version lock, or a module.
PROMPT GATE SHAPE: this prompt's own gate builds ONLY :android (:android:assembleDebug / lintDebug /
    ktlintCheck / detekt / testDebugUnitTest). It never builds a :wear module — consistent with no wearable
    module being in scope.

=== REASONING (chosen approach + rejected alternatives) ===
A) Build a real :wear module (Wear Compose + Horologist + Wear Data Layer). REJECTED — those artifacts are
   not in the ADR-012 locked catalog; adding them floats versions / introduces a new major dependency stack,
   which ADR-012 forbids without a SUPERSEDING ADR. apps/versions.lock.md and the ADRs are OUTSIDE this
   prompt's Allowed files (apps/android/** + log), so locking the deps or authoring an ADR here would be a
   Rule 9 (silent drift) + Rule 2 (scope) violation. The prompt's gate also never builds :wear.
B) Ship a minimal Wear shell / skeleton to "satisfy" the artifact. REJECTED — forbidden verbatim by the
   prompt ("do not create a fake shell") and by Honesty Covenant rules 4 (no stubs) & 5 (no parity shortcuts).
C) Mark NOT-APPLICABLE / BLOCKED with evidence and author ZERO Wear code. CHOSEN — this is the outcome the
   prompt explicitly sanctions when Wear is out of scope in the parity ledger. The authoritative scope
   (ADR-002 platform matrix + the parity manifest with no wearable unit + the ADR-012 lock with no Wear deps)
   places a native Wear OS companion out of scope; the watch FEATURE's Android parity is owned by the A7
   phone page + the shared-core WatchStore.

=== DECISION ===
WEAR_OS_COMPANION=NOT_APPLICABLE (out of platform scope)
PRIMARY_BASIS=ADR-002 platform matrix excludes Wear OS + parity-manifest.json has no wearable unit +
    ADR-012/versions.lock.md lock no Wear Compose/Horologist/Data Layer + this prompt's Allowed-files & gate
    (only :android, lock file & ADRs out of scope).
SECONDARY_BASIS=Rule 7 predecessor — the "relevant A7 watch page" (pages/watch/WatchFacePage.prompt.md) is
    not DONE (log absent; no watch screen in the app), so there is no in-repo Android watch surface for a
    companion to mirror / Data-Layer-sync with.
ACTION=author ZERO Wear code — no :wear module, no stub Composable, no version-catalog edit, no fake shell.
MARKER=WearOsOutOfPlatformScopeByADR002

